vibe-lang's patch for z3's hardware floats (mizchi/vibe-lang#3883, scripts/z3_wasi/z3.patch, made
for z3 4.15.8; src/util/hwf.cpp is the same file in 4.16.0, so it applies unchanged).

z3 sets the rounding mode of the CPU's floats with fesetround. WebAssembly has one rounding mode,
to nearest with ties to even, so wasi-libc's fenv.h for wasm32 defines FE_TONEAREST and no other
mode, and the file doesn't compile. On WASI the patch keeps that one mode and makes every other one
unreachable: z3 stops with an error where it would otherwise round to nearest in place of the mode
it asked for. lengua asks z3 no questions with floats; cvc5 answers those.

diff --git a/src/util/hwf.cpp b/src/util/hwf.cpp
index 52ba280..9496c0d 100644
--- a/src/util/hwf.cpp
+++ b/src/util/hwf.cpp
@@ -588,6 +588,15 @@ void hwf_manager::set_rounding_mode(mpf_rounding_mode rm)
         UNREACHABLE(); // Note: MPF_ROUND_NEAREST_TAWAY is not supported by the hardware!
     }
 #endif
+#elif defined(__wasi__)
+    // wasm has round-to-nearest-even only (no fesetround modes): any other
+    // mode is unreachable rather than silently computed at nearest.
+    switch (rm) {
+    case MPF_ROUND_NEAREST_TEVEN:
+        break;
+    default:
+        UNREACHABLE();
+    }
 #else // macOS/Linux
     switch (rm) {
     case MPF_ROUND_NEAREST_TEVEN:
